t-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>30</text><text x='390' y='56' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>108°</text><text x='240' y='78' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='start'>Rent</text><text x='335' y='78' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>25</text><text x='390' y='78' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>90°</text><text x='240' y='100' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='start'>Savings</text><text x='335' y='100' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>20</text><text x='390' y='100' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>72°</text><text x='240' y='122' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='start'>Education</text><text x='335' y='122' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>15</text><text x='390' y='122' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>54°</text><text x='240' y='144' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='start'>Travel</text><text x='335' y='144' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>10</text><text x='390' y='144' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>36°</text><line x1='240' y1='40' x2='420' y2='40' stroke='#9fb3ae'/><text x='330' y='178' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>whole circle = 100% = 360°</text><text x='330' y='194' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#D95D39' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>so 1% = 3.6°</text></svg></div>
<div class="rule">Pie chart: 100% = 360°, so 1% = 3.6°<small>angle = % × 3.6 · % = angle ÷ 3.6 · a 90° sector is 25%</small></div>
<div class='yt'><div class='yth'>✎ Your turn</div><ol><li>From the bar chart: by what % did sales rise from Wednesday to Thursday?</li><li>From the bar chart: find the average daily sales.</li><li>From the pie: if the family spends ₹60,000 a month, how much goes to Savings? What % is a 54° sector?</li></ol><div class='yta'>Answers: 1. 90 → 180, rise 90 ÷ 90 = 100% · 2. 700 ÷ 5 = 140 cups · 3. 20% of 60,000 = ₹12,000; 54 ÷ 3.6 = 15%</div></div>

<h2><span class="n">20.5</span>Timed sets: five questions in 8 minutes</h2>
<p>In the exam, one table usually carries five questions. Think of the set as one job of about 8 minutes, not five separate jobs. A cricket captain sets the field once for the whole over, not again for every ball. In the same way, you read the table once and work out the shared numbers once.</p>
