xt><line x1='20.0' y1='68' x2='20.0' y2='76' stroke='#17423B'/><text x='20.0' y='90' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>0</text><line x1='72.5' y1='68' x2='72.5' y2='76' stroke='#17423B'/><text x='72.5' y='90' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>1</text><line x1='125.0' y1='68' x2='125.0' y2='76' stroke='#17423B'/><text x='125.0' y='90' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>2</text><line x1='177.5' y1='68' x2='177.5' y2='76' stroke='#17423B'/><text x='177.5' y='90' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>3</text><line x1='230.0' y1='68' x2='230.0' y2='76' stroke='#17423B'/><text x='230.0' y='90' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>4</text><line x1='282.5' y1='68' x2='282.5' y2='76' stroke='#17423B'/><text x='282.5' y='90' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>5</text><line x1='335.0' y1='68' x2='335.0' y2='76' stroke='#17423B'/><text x='335.0' y='90' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>6</text><line x1='387.5' y1='68' x2='387.5' y2='76' stroke='#17423B'/><text x='387.5' y='90' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>7</text><line x1='440.0' y1='68' x2='440.0' y2='76' stroke='#17423B'/><text x='440.0' y='90' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>8</text><text x='230' y='14' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12.5' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>One DI set: 5 questions in 8 minutes</text><text x='230' y='108' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11' fill='#1B2A2F' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>minutes</text></svg></div>
<div class="rule">Read all five questions first. Then calculate the shared totals once. Then solve the easiest first.<small>If any one question takes more than 2 minutes, mark it and move on</small></div>
<p><b>Speed habits.</b> Write row or column totals in the margin when two questions need them. Round boldly when the options are far apart. And know these fractions as percentages, so that a division becomes a quick look-up:</p>
<table class="data"><tr><th><span class="fr"><span>1</span><span>2</span></span></th><th><span class="fr"><span>1</span><span>3</span></span></th><th><span class="fr"><span>1</span><span>4</span></span></th><th><span class="fr"><span>1</span><span>5</span></span></th><th><span class="fr"><span>1</span><span>6</span></span></th><th><span class="fr"><span>1</span><span>8</span></span></th><th><span class="fr"><span>1</span><span>9</span></span></th><th><span class="fr"><span>1</span><span>12</span></span></th></tr><tr><td>50%</td><td>33.3%</td><td>25%</td><td>20%</td><td>16.7%</td><td>12.5%</td><td>11.1%</td><td>8.3%</td></tr></table>
<div class="chat"><div class="cb"><div class="av" style="background:#F2A541;color:#17423B">A</div><div class="bub"><b>Ayesha:</b> "Which year had the lowest average marks?" Do I really need five divisions?</div></div><div class="cb right"><div class="av" style="background:#5b6b6f;color:#fff">✎</div><div class="bub"><b>Teacher:</b> No. Every year has the same five students, so the lowest total is also the lowest average. Speed comes from doing less work.</div></div></div>
<div class='yt'><div class='yth'>✎ Your turn</div><ol><li>Sales (₹ lakh) of three shops are given below. Set your timer for 3 minutes. (a) Which year had the highest total sales? (b) Y's 2025 sales were what % less than its 2024 sales? (c) What were X's average sales over the three years?<table class="data"><tr><th>Shop</th><th>2023</th><th>2024</th><th>2025</th></tr><tr><td>X</td><td>40</td><td>50</td><td>60</td></tr><tr><td>Y</td><td>30</td><td>45</td><td>36</td></tr><tr><td>Z</td><td>50</td><td>55</td><td>45</td></tr></table></li></ol><div class='yta'>Answers: (a) totals 120, 150, 141 → 2024 · (b) 9 ÷ 45 = 20% · (c) 150 ÷ 3 = ₹50 lakh</div></div>

<h2><span class="n">20.6</span>How to handle any table or chart set</h2>
<div class="steps3"><div><b>1. Read the questions</b>All five, before the table. Note which numbers repeat.</div><div><b>2. Build what you need</b>Girls and boys, expenditure, or values read from a chart. Work them out once, in a small table.</div><div><b>3. Calculate and move</b>Use the five calculations. Round when allowed. Mark and skip any slow one.</div></div>
<div class="fig"><svg viewBox='0 0 460 300' width='100%' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'><line x1='230' y1='150' x2='80' y2='40' stroke='#F2A541' stroke-width='3'/><line x1='230' y1='150' x2='380' y2='40' stroke='#F2A541' stroke-width='3'/><line x1='230' y1='150' x2='65' y2='150' stroke='#F2A541' stroke-width='3'/><line x1='230' y1='150' x2='395' y2='150' stroke='#F2A541' stroke-width='3'/><line x1='230' y1='150' x2='80' y2='260' stroke='#F2A541' stroke-width='3'/><line x1='230' y1='150' x2='380' y2='260' stroke='#F2A541' stroke-width='3'/><circle cx='230' cy='150' r='48' fill='#17423B'/><text x='230' y='147.5' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='14' fill='#fff' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>TABLES AND</text><text x='230' y='164.5' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='14' fill='#fff' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>CHARTS</text><rect x='8' y='16' width='144' height='48' rx='10' fill='#fff' stroke='#17423B' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='80' y='36' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='13' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>Total and %</text><text x='80' y='54' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#1B2A2F' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>part = total × %</text><rect x='308' y='16' width='144' height='48' rx='10' fill='#fff' stroke='#17423B' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='380' y='36' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='13' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>The other part</text><text x='380' y='54' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#1B2A2F' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>(100 − %) of total</text><rect x='-7' y='126' width='144' height='48' rx='10' fill='#fff' stroke='#17423B' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='65' y='146' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='13' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>Profit table</text><text x='65' y='164' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#1B2A2F' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>E = I ÷ (1 + p%)</text><rect x='323' y='126' width='144' height='48' rx='10' fill='#fff' stroke='#17423B' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='395' y='146' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='13' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>Median</text><text x='395' y='164' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#1B2A2F' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>sort, then middle</text><rect x='8' y='236' width='144' height='48' rx='10' fill='#fff' stroke='#17423B' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='80' y='256' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='13' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>Pie chart</text><text x='80' y='274' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#1B2A2F' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>1% = 3.6°</text><rect x='308' y='236' width='144' height='48' rx='10' fill='#fff' stroke='#17423B' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='380' y='256' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='13' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>Timed set</text><text x='380' y='274' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#1B2A2F' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>5 questions, 8 min</text></svg></div><p class="cap">The whole chapter on one page. Revise from here before the exam.</p>
<div class="card"><h4>Quick card</h4><table><tr><td>Part from total</td><td>total × % ÷ 100; other part = total − part</td></tr><tr><td>Expenditure</td><td>income ÷ (1 + profit % ÷ 100)</td></tr><tr><td>Income</td><td>expenditure × (1 + profit % ÷ 100)</td></tr><tr><td>Median</td><td>sort first; middle value, or average of the two middle</td></tr><tr><td>Pie chart</td><td>1% = 3.6°; angle ÷ 3.6 = %</td></tr><tr><td>Timed set</td><td>5 questions in about 8 minutes; skip after 2 minutes</td></tr></table></div></div>$less$ where no = 20;
update public.course_chapters set lesson_html = $less$<div class="pD"><div class="opener"><div class="k">Part D - Exam Formats · Chapter 21</div><h1>Statement and Match Formats</h1><div class="sub">Using the options to solve faster</div></div>
<p>Some questions in Paper 1 give you four statements and ask which are correct, or two lists to match. They look like four questions packed into one, but the options themselves give you most of the answer, and the maths inside comes from chapters you have already done. You will meet 12 real past questions here.</p>
<div class="chal"><div class="chh">⏱ 10-second challenge</div><div>At a quiz in Mysuru the options are (1) A and B only, (2) A and C only, (3) B and D only, (4) A, B and D only. Neha is sure that statement A is false. Which option is the answer?</div><div class="chw">Make a quick guess. The answer is in section 21.2.</div></div>
<div class="goals"><h4>By the end of this chapter you will be able to</h4><ul><li>read the options first and see which combinations are possible;</li><li>solve "which statements are correct" questions by checking the easiest statement first;</li><li>solve match-the-list questions by elimination, usually with two rows;</li><li>answer Statement I / Statement II questions without confusion;</li><li>know which earlier chapter to use for each kind of statement.</li></ul></div>


<h2><span class="n">21.1</span>One question, four small questions</h2>
<p>Think of Anjali, a ticket checker on a train to Bhubaneswar. She does not read every line of your ticket. She looks at the date and the train number. If one of them is wrong, the ticket is wrong, and she does not need the rest. Statement and match questions can be checked in the same way.</p>
<div class="fig"><svg viewBox='0 0 460 166' width='100%' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'><defs><marker id='ah' markerWidth='8' markerHeight='8' refX='6' refY='3' orient='auto'><path d='M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 z' fill='#17423B'/></marker><marker id='ar' markerWidth='8' markerHeight='8' refX='6' refY='3' orient='auto'><path d='M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 z' fill='#D95D39'/></marker></defs><rect x='150' y='6' width='160' height='34' rx='6' fill='#17423B'/><text x='230' y='28' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='13' fill='#fff' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>One exam question</text><line x1='230' y1='42' x2='65' y2='70' stroke='#17423B' stroke-width='2' marker-end='url(#ah)'/><rect x='20' y='74' width='90' height='44' rx='6' fill='#fff' stroke='#17423B' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='50' y='101' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>mini Q A</text><text x='94' y='102' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='16' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>✓</text><line x1='230' y1='42' x2='175' y2='70' stroke='#17423B' stroke-width='2' marker-end='url(#ah)'/><rect x='130' y='74' width='90' height='44' rx='6' fill='#fff' stroke='#D95D39' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='160' y='101' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>mini Q B</text><text x='204' y='102' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='16' fill='#D95D39' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>✗</text><line x1='230' y1='42' x2='285' y2='70' stroke='#17423B' stroke-width='2' marker-end='url(#ah)'/><rect x='240' y='74' width='90' height='44' rx='6' fill='#EEF4F2' stroke='#9fb3ae' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='270' y='101' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>mini Q C</text><text x='314' y='102' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='16' fill='#9fb3ae' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>?</text><line x1='230' y1='42' x2='395' y2='70' stroke='#17423B' stroke-width='2' marker-end='url(#ah)'/><rect x='350' y='74' width='90' height='44' rx='6' fill='#EEF4F2' stroke='#9fb3ae' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='380' y='101' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>mini Q D</text><text x='424' y='102' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='16' fill='#9fb3ae' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>?</text><text x='230' y='142' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>Each statement or row is a small question of its own.</text><text x='230' y='158' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#1B2A2F' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>Often two of them are enough: the options decide the rest.</text></svg></div>
<div class="rule">Read the four options before you solve anything<small>They tell you which statements or rows actually matter</small></div>
<p>Notice the size of the job. Four statements can be true or false in 16 different ways, but the question offers only four options. So one statement you check can remove two or three options at once.</p>

<h2><span class="n">21.2</span>Which statements are correct?</h2>
<p>Let us take an example and solve it the smart way.</p>
<div class="ex"><span class="t">Example.</span> Which of the following statements are correct?<br>A. 15% of 240 is 36.<br>B. 1 ÷ 0.25 = 0.4<br>C. The average of 4, 8 and 12 is 8.<br>D. A speed of 36 km/h is 10 m/s.<br>(1) A and B only &nbsp; (2) A, C and D only &nbsp; (3) B and C only &nbsp; (4) A, B, C and D<p>Start with the quickest statement. B takes two seconds: 1 ÷ 0.25 = 100 ÷ 25 = 4, not 0.4. So B is false. Cross out every option that contains B: options 1, 3 and 4 go. Only option <b>(2)</b> is left. We checked one statement out of four.</p></div>
<div class="rule">Check the easiest statement first. If it is false, strike out every option that has it.<small>If it is true, strike out every option that does not have it.</small></div>
<div class="rev"><b>⏱ Challenge answer:</b> option (3). A is false, so every option containing A goes: 1, 2 and 4. Only (3), B and D, is left, and Neha checked nothing else.</div>
<div class='trap'><b>⚠ Exam trap:</b> read the question word. "Which are <b>correct</b>?" and "Which are <b>wrong</b>?" have opposite answers. Underline the word before you start. A true statement belongs in the answer of the first kind, and a false one in the answer of the second kind.</div>
<div class='yt'><div class='yth'>✎ Your turn</div><ol><li>Which statements are <b>wrong</b>?<br>A. <span class="fr"><span>3</span><span>8</span></span> = 37.5% &nbsp; B. 2⁵ = 25 &nbsp; C. √144 = 12 &nbsp; D. 20% of 50 = 25% of 40<br>(1) B only &nbsp; (2) B and D only &nbsp; (3) A and B only &nbsp; (4) C only</li></ol><div class='yta'>Answers: B is wrong (2⁵ = 32), so option 4 goes. D: 10 = 10, true, so option 2 goes. A: 3 ÷ 8 = 0.375, true, so option 3 goes. Answer (1)</div></div>

<h2><span class="n">21.3</span>Match the list</h2>
<p>A match question is like matching each child in a class photo to a name. You do not start with the child you are unsure about. You start with the one you know at once. Here is a full example.</p>
<div class="ex"><span class="t">Example.</span> Match List-I with List-II.<br>A. 20% of 150 → I. 9<br>B. √81 → II. 30<br>C. Average of 10, 20, 30, 40 → III. 25<br>D. 1 ÷ 0.05 → IV. 20<br>Options: (1) A-II, B-I, C-III, D-IV &nbsp; (2) A-III, B-I, C-II, D-IV &nbsp; (3) A-II, B-IV, C-III, D-I &nbsp; (4) A-IV, B-II, C-III, D-I</div>
<div class="fig"><svg viewBox='0 0 460 208' width='100%' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'><rect x='130' y='4' width='74' height='160' rx='4' fill='#FBE7C6'/><text x='94' y='20' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>Row A</text><text x='166' y='20' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>Row B</text><text x='238' y='20' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>Row C</text><text x='310' y='20' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>Row D</text><text x='32' y='49' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='13' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>(1)</text><rect x='60' y='30' width='68' height='26' rx='4' fill='#fff' stroke='#9fb3ae' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='94' y='48' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12.5' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>A-II</text><rect x='132' y='30' width='68' height='26' rx='4' fill='#fff' stroke='#9fb3ae' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='166' y='48' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12.5' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>B-I</text><rect x='204' y='30' width='68' height='26' rx='4' fill='#fff' stroke='#9fb3ae' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='238' y='48' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12.5' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>C-III</text><rect x='276' y='30' width='68' height='26' rx='4' fill='#fff' stroke='#9fb3ae' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='310' y='48' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12.5' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>D-IV</text><text x='356' y='48' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='start'>✓ the answer</text><text x='32' y='82' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='13' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>(2)</text><rect x='60' y='63' width='68' height='26' rx='4' fill='#fff' stroke='#9fb3ae' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='94' y='81' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12.5' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>A-III</text><rect x='132' y='63' width='68' height='26' rx='4' fill='#fff' stroke='#9fb3ae' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='166' y='81' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12.5' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>B-I</text><rect x='204' y='63' width='68' height='26' rx='4' fill='#fff' stroke='#9fb3ae' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='238' y='81' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12.5' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>C-II</text><rect x='276' y='63' width='68' height='26' rx='4' fill='#fff' stroke='#9fb3ae' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='310' y='81' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12.5' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>D-IV</text><line x1='56' y1='76' x2='348' y2='76' stroke='#D95D39' stroke-width='2'/><text x='356' y='81' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11' fill='#D95D39' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='start'>✗ A-III is wrong</text><text x='32' y='115' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='13' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>(3)</text><rect x='60' y='96' width='68' height='26' rx='4' fill='#fff' stroke='#9fb3ae' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='94' y='114' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12.5' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>A-II</text><rect x='132' y='96' width='68' height='26' rx='4' fill='#fff' stroke='#9fb3ae' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='166' y='114' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12.5' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>B-IV</text><rect x='204' y='96' width='68' height='26' rx='4' fill='#fff' stroke='#9fb3ae' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='238' y='114' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12.5' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>C-III</text><rect x='276' y='96' width='68' height='26' rx='4' fill='#fff' stroke='#9fb3ae' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='310' y='114' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12.5' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>D-I</text><line x1='56' y1='109' x2='348' y2='109' stroke='#D95D39' stroke-width='2'/><text x='356' y='114' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11' fill='#D95D39' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='start'>✗ B-IV is wrong</text><text x='32' y='148' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='13' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>(4)</text><rect x='60' y='129' width='68' height='26' rx='4' fill='#fff' stroke='#9fb3ae' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='94' y='147' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12.5' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>A-IV</text><rect x='132' y='129' width='68' height='26' rx='4' fill='#fff' stroke='#9fb3ae' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='166' y='147' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12.5' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>B-II</text><rect x='204' y='129' width='68' height='26' rx='4' fill='#fff' stroke='#9fb3ae' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='238' y='147' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12.5' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>C-III</text><rect x='276' y='129' width='68' height='26' rx='4' fill='#fff' stroke='#9fb3ae' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='310' y='147' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12.5' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>D-I</text><line x1='56' y1='142' x2='348' y2='142' stroke='#D95D39' stroke-width='2'/><text x='356' y='147' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11' fill='#D95D39' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='start'>✗ B-II is wrong</text><text x='230' y='184' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>Step 1: √81 = 9, so B-I. Options 3 and 4 go.</text><text x='230' y='201' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>Step 2: 20% of 150 = 30, so A-II. Option 2 goes. Done.</text></svg></div>
<div class="rule">Solve the easiest row. Keep only the options that agree. Then the next easiest row among those left.<small>Two rows usually decide the answer</small></div>
<div class="chat"><div class="cb"><div class="av" style="background:#17423B;color:#fff">T</div><div class="bub"><b>Tenzin:</b> Should I always start with the row I find easiest?</div></div><div class="cb right"><div class="av" style="background:#5b6b6f;color:#fff">✎</div><div class="bub"><b>Teacher:</b> Start with an easy row that splits the options. Row C is C-III in options 1, 3 and 4, so it removes only one. Row B splits them two and two.</div></div></div>
<div class='yt'><div class='yth'>✎ Your turn</div><ol><li>Match List-I with List-II:<br>A. 25% of 64 → I. 6 &nbsp; B. ∛216 → II. 16 &nbsp; C. <span class="fr"><span>3</span><span>4</span></span> of 32 → III. 12 &nbsp; D. average of 8, 12, 16 → IV. 24<br>(1) A-II, B-I, C-IV, D-III &nbsp; (2) A-I, B-II, C-IV, D-III &nbsp; (3) A-II, B-III, C-I, D-IV &nbsp; (4) A-IV, B-I, C-II, D-III</li></ol><div class='yta'>Answers: B: 6 × 6 × 6 = 216, so B-I: options 1 and 4 remain. A: 64 ÷ 4 = 16, so A-II: only option (1). Check: C = 24 (IV), D = 12 (III)</div></div>

<h2><span class="n">21.4</span>Statement I and Statement II</h2>
<p>Here there are only two statements, and the four options are always the same four boxes. Judge each statement on its own, then find its box.</p>
<div class="fig"><svg viewBox='0 0 460 178' width='100%' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'><text x='280' y='16' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>Statement II</text><text x='215' y='36' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>correct</text><text x='345' y='36' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>incorrect</text><text x='60' y='66' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>Statement I</text><text x='60' y='80' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>correct</text><text x='60' y='120' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>Statement I</text><text x='60' y='134' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#17423B' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>incorrect</text><rect x='150' y='46' width='128' height='48' rx='6' fill='#17423B' stroke='#fff' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='214' y='75' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#fff' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>Both correct</text><rect x='280' y='46' width='128' height='48' rx='6' fill='#F2A541' stroke='#fff' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='344' y='75' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>I correct, II incorrect</text><rect x='150' y='100' width='128' height='48' rx='6' fill='#F2A541' stroke='#fff' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='214' y='129' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>I incorrect, II correct</text><rect x='280' y='100' width='128' height='48' rx='6' fill='#EEF4F2' stroke='#fff' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='344' y='129' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>Both incorrect</text><text x='230' y='170' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>Judge each statement alone. Then find its box.</text></svg></div>
<div class="ex"><span class="t">Example.</span> Statement I: The sum of the whole numbers from 1 to 20 is 210. Statement II: If the side of a square is doubled, its area is doubled.<p>I: there are 20 numbers and their average is (1 + 20) ÷ 2 = 10.5, so the sum is 20 × 10.5 = 210. Correct. II: a square of side 1 has area 1; a square of side 2 has area 4. The area becomes 4 times. Incorrect. Answer: <b>I correct, II incorrect</b>.</p></div>
<div class='think'><b>💡 Think of it like this:</b> a quick example with small numbers is the fastest test of a general statement. To test "the area doubles", try a side of 1 and a side of 2. One example that fails is enough to call a statement incorrect.</div>
<div class='yt'><div class='yth'>✎ Your turn</div><ol><li>Statement I: 0.3 × 0.3 = 0.9. Statement II: Kiran drives at 50 km/h, so she covers 175 km in 3 hours 30 minutes.</li></ol><div class='yta'>Answers: I: 0.3 × 0.3 = 0.09, incorrect. II: 50 × 3.5 = 175, correct. Answer: I incorrect, II correct</div></div>

<h2><span class="n">21.5</span>Your toolkit: the maths inside the statements</h2>
<p>The statements can come from any chapter of this book. When a statement looks unfamiliar, ask which chapter it belongs to, and use the method from there.</p>
<table class="data" style="break-inside: avoid"><tr><th>If the statement is about ...</th><th>Revise</th></tr><tr><td>fractions, decimals, percentages</td><td>Chapters 1 to 4</td></tr><tr><td>profit, discount, interest</td><td>Chapters 5 to 7</td></tr><tr><td>ratio, averages, sums of numbers</td><td>Chapters 8 and 9</td></tr><tr><td>speed, trains, work</td><td>Chapters 10 and 11</td></tr><tr><td>powers, roots, area, clocks</td><td>Chapters 12 and 13</td></tr><tr><td>series, coding</td><td>Chapters 14 to 16</td></tr></table>
<div class="card"><h4>Four quick checks that come up often</h4><table><tr><td>km/h to m/s</td><td>× <span class="fr"><span>5</span><span>18</span></span> (so 36 km/h = 10 m/s)</td></tr><tr><td>Sum of a run of numbers</td><td>how many × average of first and last</td></tr><tr><td>a² − b²</td><td>(a − b)(a + b), so 7² − 3² = 4 × 10 = 40</td></tr><tr><td>Area when side × k</td><td>area × k²</td></tr></table></div>
<div class='yt'><div class='yth'>✎ Your turn</div><ol><li>Find the sum of the whole numbers from 11 to 30.</li><li>Change 72 km/h into m/s.</li><li>Find 51² − 49² without squaring.</li></ol><div class='yta'>Answers: 1. 20 numbers × average 20.5 = 410 · 2. 72 × <span class="fr"><span>5</span><span>18</span></span> = 20 m/s · 3. (51 − 49)(51 + 49) = 2 × 100 = 200</div></div>

<h2><span class="n">21.6</span>How to solve any statement or match question</h2>
<div class="steps3"><div><b>1. Options first</b>Read the four options. Underline "correct" or "wrong".</div><div><b>2. Easiest first</b>Solve the quickest statement or the row that splits the options. Strike out.</div><div><b>3. Stop early</b>When one option is left, mark it and move on. Check another row only if time allows.</div></div>
<div class="fig"><svg viewBox='0 0 460 300' width='100%' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'><line x1='230' y1='150' x2='80' y2='40' stroke='#F2A541' stroke-width='3'/><line x1='230' y1='150' x2='380' y2='40' stroke='#F2A541' stroke-width='3'/><line x1='230' y1='150' x2='65' y2='150' stroke='#F2A541' stroke-width='3'/><line x1='230' y1='150' x2='395' y2='150' stroke='#F2A541' stroke-width='3'/><line x1='230' y1='150' x2='80' y2='260' stroke='#F2A541' stroke-width='3'/><line x1='230' y1='150' x2='380' y2='260' stroke='#F2A541' stroke-width='3'/><circle cx='230' cy='150' r='48' fill='#17423B'/><text x='230' y='147.5' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='14' fill='#fff' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>STATEMENT</text><text x='230' y='164.5' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='14' fill='#fff' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>AND MATCH</text><rect x='8' y='16' width='144' height='48' rx='10' fill='#fff' stroke='#17423B' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='80' y='36' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='13' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>Options first</text><text x='80' y='54' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#1B2A2F' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>see what can happen</text><rect x='308' y='16' width='144' height='48' rx='10' fill='#fff' stroke='#17423B' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='380' y='36' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='13' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>Easiest first</text><text x='380' y='54' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#1B2A2F' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>seconds, not minutes</text><rect x='-7' y='126' width='144' height='48' rx='10' fill='#fff' stroke='#17423B' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='65' y='146' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='13' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>Cross out</text><text x='65' y='164' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#1B2A2F' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>false: strike them all</text><rect x='323' y='126' width='144' height='48' rx='10' fill='#fff' stroke='#17423B' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='395' y='146' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='13' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>Stop early</text><text x='395' y='164' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#1B2A2F' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>one option left</text><rect x='8' y='236' width='144' height='48' rx='10' fill='#fff' stroke='#17423B' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='80' y='256' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='13' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>Read the verb</text><text x='80' y='274' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#1B2A2F' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>correct or wrong?</text><rect x='308' y='236' width='144' height='48' rx='10' fill='#fff' stroke='#17423B' stroke-width='1.3'/><text x='380' y='256' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='13' fill='#17423B' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle'>I and II</text><text x='380' y='274' font-family='Carlito,Calibri,sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#1B2A2F' font-weight='normal' text-anchor='middle'>judge each alone</text></svg></div><p class="cap">The whole chapter on one page. Revise from here before the exam.</p>
<div class="card"><h4>Quick card</h4><table><tr><td>Statement-type</td><td>easiest statement first; false → strike every option with it</td></tr><tr><td>Match the list</td><td>easiest row first; keep options that agree</td></tr><tr><td>Choosing a row</td><td>the one whose value differs most across options</td></tr><tr><td>Statement I / II</td><td>judge each alone, then pick the box</td></tr><tr><td>General statement</td><td>test it with small numbers</td></tr><tr><td>"Wrong" questions</td><td>you are looking for the false ones</td></tr></table></div></div>$less$ where no = 21;
commit;
-- VERIFY: expect 21
select count(*) as chapters_with_lessons from public.course_chapters where lesson_html is not null;
